    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The narrative centers on accelerating AI adoption, with AI-related work becoming a major revenue contributor and growing rapidly. The Technology, Media, and Telecom vertical is the primary growth engine, driving outsized year-on-year expansion. While overall demand for digital transformation remains healthy, the near-term outlook is mixed—full-year expectations were raised above Wall Street’s view, yet next-quarter guidance came in slightly soft, hinting at uneven project ramps or cautious client spending. Concerns linger around margin pressures, as the rapid mix shift toward AI and diversification efforts appear to carry elevated cost structures.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a deliberate AI-led growth strategy, steering the company to a record share of AI revenue and successfully diversifying beyond its historical client concentration. The team demonstrated operational credibility by delivering revenue above the high end of its own guidance and lifting the full-year top-line outlook. However, the GAAP net loss and a softer near-term revenue guide introduce caution, suggesting that scaling the AI practice is straining profitability in the short run. Overall, management is hitting its strategic targets but faces questions about balancing growth investments with sustainable earnings.",
